# Everything in the repo is site content and gets served, EXCEPT what is listed
# here. Anything added to the repo that is not meant to be public — internal
# notes, build tooling, deploy config — must be added to this list.
#
# config/ is the one exception that stays in the context: the Dockerfile needs
# config/nginx.conf, and .dockerignore would put it out of reach. The Dockerfile
# deletes it from the served root instead.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.kamal
config/deploy.yml
docs
README.md
CONTENT-TODO.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Unprocessed originals and retired brand art. Kept in git on purpose (they are
# B9's photographs and the raw material for every derivative in images/), but no
# page links to them, so shipping them was 27 MB of dead weight in a 28 MB image
# and a 16 MB PNG anyone could pull off the public site.
#
# The rule: images/ is what the site serves, images/source/ is what it was made
# from. Process an original into images/ or images/web/ and link it from a page
# and it ships. No enumeration, same as the COPY it replaced.
images/source
